@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "koroneiki"

Feature: Koroneiki Product API Permissioning
	Testing Koroneiki Product API Permissioning functionality.

Teardown:
	* I tear down the permissions for a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" set for a non permissioned user
	* I tear down the permissions for a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Portal Six" set for a non permissioned user
	* I tear down the products on koroneiki with the following names
	| Liferay Digital Experience Platform |
	| Liferay Portal Six                  |

Scenario: Create product attempt by non permissioned user
	Koroneiki products that are attempted to be created via API by non permissioned users should not be created.

	Given I attempt to create a product with the following values as a non permissioned user
	| Name | Liferay Digital Experience Platform | |
	Then I should not be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform"

Scenario: View product attempt by non permissioned user
	Koroneiki products should not be viewable for non permissioned users.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | Liferay Digital Experience Platform | |
	Then I should not be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" as a non permissioned user

Scenario: Update product attempt by non permissioned user
	Koroneiki products that are attempted to be updated via API by non permissioned users should not be updated.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | Liferay Digital Experience Platform | |
	And I attempt to update a product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" to have the following values as a non permissioned user
	| Name | Liferay Portal Six | |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" and the following values
	| Name | Liferay Digital Experience Platform | |
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Portal Six"
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" as a non permissioned user

Scenario: Remove product attempt by non permissioned user
	Koroneiki products removed via API should not be viewable via API by non permissioned users.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | Liferay Digital Experience Platform | |
	And I attempt to delete a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" as a non permissioned user
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" and the following values
	| Name | Liferay Digital Experience Platform | |
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" as a non permissioned user

Scenario: Create product external link attempt by non permissioned user
	Koroneiki product external links should not be able to be created via API by non permissioned users.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | Liferay Digital Experience Platform | |
	And I attempt to create an external link on a product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" with the following values as a non permissioned user
	| Domain      | liferaydxp |
	| Entity Id   | 1234       |
	| Entity Name | LiferayDXP |
	Then the external link with the entity id "1234" should not be present on the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform"

Scenario: View product external link attempt by non permissioned user
	Koroneiki product external links should not be viewable by non permissioned users.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | Liferay Digital Experience Platform | |
	And I create an external link on a product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" with the following values
	| Domain      | liferaydxp |
	| Entity Id   | 1234       |
	| Entity Name | LiferayDXP |
	Then the external link with the entity id "1234" should be present on the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" with the following values
	| Domain      | liferaydxp |
	| Entity Id   | 1234       |
	| Entity Name | LiferayDXP |
	And the external link with the entity id "1234" on the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" should not be visible to a non permissioned user
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" using the external link domain "liferaydxp" and entity name "LiferayDXP" and entity id "1234" as a non permissioned user

Scenario: Remove product external link attempt by non permissioned user
	Koroneiki product external links should not be removable by non permissioned users.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | Liferay Digital Experience Platform | |
	And I create an external link on a product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" with the following values
	| Domain      | liferaydxp |
	| Entity Id   | 1234       |
	| Entity Name | LiferayDXP |
	And I attempt to delete an external link with the entity id "1234" on the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" as a non permissioned user
	Then the external link with the entity id "1234" should be present on the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" with the following values
	| Domain      | liferaydxp |
	| Entity Id   | 1234       |
	| Entity Name | LiferayDXP |
	And the external link with the entity id "1234" on the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" should not be visible to a non permissioned user
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" using the external link domain "liferaydxp" and entity name "LiferayDXP" and entity id "1234" as a non permissioned user

Scenario: Set product permission attempt by non permissioned user
	Koroneiki product permissions should not be able to be set by non permissioned users.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | Liferay Digital Experience Platform | |
	And I attempt to set the permissions for a product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" to have the following values for a non permissioned user as a non permissioned user
	| Update | true |
	| View   | true |
	And I attempt to update a product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" to have the following values as a non permissioned user
	| Name | Liferay Portal Six | |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" and the following values
	| Name | Liferay Digital Experience Platform | |
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Portal Six"
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" as a non permissioned user

Scenario: Unset product permission attempt by non permissioned user
	Koroneiki product permissions should not be able to be unset by non permissioned users.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | Liferay Digital Experience Platform | |
	And I set the permissions for a product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" to have the following values for a non permissioned user
	| Update | true |
	| View   | true |
	And I attempt to unset the following permissions for a product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" for a permissioned user as a non permissioned user
	| Update | true |
	| View   | true |
	And I update a product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" to have the following values as a permissioned user
	| Name | Liferay Portal Six | |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Portal Six" and the following values
	| Name | Liferay Portal Six | |
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform"
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Portal Six" and the following values as a permissioned user
	| Name | Liferay Portal Six | |

Scenario: View product by permissioned user
	Koroneiki products should be viewable for permissioned users.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | Liferay Digital Experience Platform | |
	And I set the permissions for a product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" to have the following values for a non permissioned user
	| View | true |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" and the following values as a permissioned user
	| Name | Liferay Digital Experience Platform | |

Scenario: Update product by permissioned user
	Koroneiki products should be able to be updated by permissioned users.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | Liferay Digital Experience Platform | |
	And I set the permissions for a product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" to have the following values for a non permissioned user
	| Update | true |
	And I update a product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" to have the following values as a permissioned user
	| Name | Liferay Portal Six | |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Portal Six" and the following values
	| Name | Liferay Portal Six | |
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform"

Scenario: Remove product by permissioned user
	Koroneiki products should be able to be removed by permissioned users.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | Liferay Digital Experience Platform | |
	And I set the permissions for a product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" to have the following values for a non permissioned user
	| Delete | true |
	And I delete a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" as a permissioned user
	Then I should not be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform"

Scenario: Set product permissions by permissioned user
	Koroneiki product permissions should be able to be set by permissioned users.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | Liferay Digital Experience Platform | |
	And I set the permissions for a product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" to have the following values for a non permissioned user
	| Permissions | true |
	And I set the permissions for a product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" to have the following values for a non permissioned user as a permissioned user
	| Update | true |
	| View   | true |
	And I update a product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" to have the following values as a permissioned user
	| Name | Liferay Portal Six | |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Portal Six" and the following values
	| Name | Liferay Portal Six | |
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform"
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Portal Six" and the following values as a permissioned user
	| Name | Liferay Portal Six | |

Scenario: Unset product permissions by permissioned user
	Koroneiki product permissions should be able to be unset by permissioned users.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | Liferay Digital Experience Platform | |
	And I set the permissions for a product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" to have the following values for a non permissioned user
	| Permissions | true |
	And I set the permissions for a product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" to have the following values for a non permissioned user as a permissioned user
	| Update | true |
	| View   | true |
	And I unset the following permissions for a product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" for a permissioned user as a permissioned user
	| Update | true |
	| View   | true |
	And I attempt to update a product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" to have the following values as a non permissioned user
	| Name | Liferay Portal Six | |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" and the following values
	| Name | Liferay Digital Experience Platform | |
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Portal Six"
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" as a non permissioned user

Scenario: View product attempt by newly non permissioned user
	Koroneiki products should not be viewable for newly non permissioned users.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | Liferay Digital Experience Platform | |
	And I set the permissions for a product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" to have the following values for a non permissioned user
	| View | true |
	And I unset the following permissions for a product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" for a permissioned user
	| View | true |
	Then I should not be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" as a non permissioned user

Scenario: Update product attempt by newly non permissioned user
	Koroneiki products that are attempted to be updated via API by newly non permissioned users should not be updated.

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | Liferay Digital Experience Platform | |
	And I set the permissions for a product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" to have the following values for a non permissioned user
	| Update | true |
	And I unset the following permissions for a product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" for a permissioned user
	| Update | true |
	And I attempt to update a product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" to have the following values as a non permissioned user
	| Name | Liferay Portal Six | |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" and the following values
	| Name | Liferay Digital Experience Platform | |
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Portal Six"
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" as a non permissioned user

Scenario: Remove product attempt by newly non permissioned user
	Koroneiki products removed via API should not be viewable via API by newly non permissioned users.

